error[L0363]: macro code ran too many steps
  --> expand/macro_steps_charge_a_string.knv:12:42
   |
12 |                   (defn main () (println (grows 400))))
   |                                          ^^^^^^^^^^^ this call passed 10000 macro steps
   |
   = note: the macro calls in one top-level form run at most 10000 steps: a function call or a `recur` costs one step per expression of the body it runs, an `expand-call` costs 64 and one per form it returns, a closure costs one step and one per binding in scope, a read of a local costs one step per newer binding in scope, and a built-in costs one step per list item it copies or reads and one for every 16 bytes of text it reads, `read-form` and `string-lines` 3 per form they build, the `escape-` built-ins one for every 16 bytes they build, `add-module-note` one for every 16 bytes its note holds, and `closest-name` one step for each pair of bytes it compares between the name and the candidates
   = help: make the macro stop, or wrap the top-level form in `(with-macro-steps 30000000 ...)`
